-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",8,{
[225]="70020DC3\n1\tTBD\t\n2\tTBD\t\n3\tTBD\t\n",
[226]="7005A72E\n1\tDestroy Orkish armour and weapons at Dursh Hûl\tDestroying the Orcs' armour and weapons at Dursh Hûl will weaken the forces here.\n2\tDestroy armour barrels (total: 3)\030Destroy weapon barrels (total: 3)\tDestroying the Orcs' armour and weapons at Dursh Hûl will weaken the forces here.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have sabotaged as much of the Orcs' equipment as you could find.\n",
[227]="70041176\n1\tCollect weapons from corsairs\tCorsairs can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown.\n2\tCollect swords from corsairs in Tarlang's Crown (total: 3)\030Collect bows from corsairs in Tarlang's Crown (total: 3)\030Collect clubs from corsairs in Tarlang's Crown (total: 2)\tCorsair raiders' swords, corsair look-outs' bows, and corsair hound-masters' clubs can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown. You have encountered well-armed corsairs in Tarlang's Crown and should claim their weaponry lest another corsair raise arms against Gondor.\n3\tDeliver the weapons to Harnion in Tarlang's Crown\tHarnion can be found alongside the road in Tarlang's Crown, to the north of Edhellond. You have taken many of the corsairs' weapons, and should now deliver them to Harnion.\n",
[228]="70066A59\n1\tFind Dardreg at the lumber camp\tGovach has asked you to find his friend Dardreg at the lumber camp north of Melgobas.\n2\tTalk to Dardreg\tYou found Dardreg at the lumber camp in Anfalas. You should talk to him.\n",
[229]="70017614\n1\tBring the gland to Veúlfur at the Twenty-first Hall\030Collect Diseased Gland\tVeúlfur is at the Twenty-first Hall. After discovering a diseased gland on the Gurvand, you plucked the item clear and must now deliver it to someone who might better understand its meaning.\n",
[230]="700001A8\n1\tTalk to Donaith\tDonaith is somewhere far to the east of Aughaire, well beyond Rammas Deluon. Eilig and his brothers in Aughaire wish you to find their long-lost uncle.\n",
[231]="700358AF\n1\tSearch for whatever may have killed the man\tWhatever killed the man on the road in the northern Writhendowns is likely nearby. You should search to the south, towards the Isingmere lake.\n2\tInvestigate the tower standing upon the island\tA tower stands alone upon an island in the northern Isingmere lake, filling you with dread when you look upon it. You should investigate the tower upon the island.\n3\tSpeak with the Daegul\tA Daegul stands upon the island in the northern Isingmere lake. You should speak with the Daegul.\n",
[232]="70035CBC\n1\tHelp Gárwig\tGárwig wishes to debate the courses of action Wildermore must take regarding the recent White Hand attacks. You should speak with Gárwig.\n2\tSpeak with Gárwig\tGárwig is in the Mead Hall of Forlaw. You should speak with Gárwig.\n",
[233]="70003246\n1\tTalk to Glamír\tGlamír is in the same ruin as Nithi. Nithi has asked you to bring the haunted skull to the Elf Glamír in the hopes that he will be able to deal with the threat it represents.\n",
[234]="700281D8\n1\tTalk to Bledhun at his encampment in the Bonevales\tBledhun's encampment is in the east of the Bonevales. You should bring the note you found to Bledhun.\n",
[235]="70068CB1\n1\tCollect palm timber ([see journal]/6)\030Repair the damaged dock planks ([see journal]/10)\tNargo asked you to harvest palm wood from the forest outside of the city and then repair the planks on the dock.\n2\tReturn to Nargo and tell him you completed his request\tYou chopped down some nearby trees to collect palm timber and repaired the planks on the dock. Return to Nargo, on the Halrax docks, with the news.\n",
[236]="70027192\n1\tSearch for signs of Dilwun's wife near the other bodies\tIf the farmer's son Dilwun had a wife, her body will surely be near the others. You should search for signs of Dilwun's wife among the others.\n2\tSearch for signs of whoever made the first footprint\tWhere you find one footprint, there must surely be another somewhere nearby. You should search the area for signs of the woman who may have lived on this farm.\n3\tSeek more footprints to track down the person who made them\tWhere you find one footprint, there must surely be another somewhere nearby. You should search the area for signs of the woman who may have lived on this farm.\n4\tSeek more footprints to track down the person who made them\tWhere you find one footprint, there must surely be another somewhere nearby. You should search the area for signs of the woman who may have lived on this farm.\n5\tSeek more footprints to track down the person who made them\tWhere you find one footprint, there must surely be another somewhere nearby. You should search the area for signs of the woman who may have lived on this farm.\n6\tTry to find whoever made the footprints that led up from the river-bank\tThe wife of Dilwun is likely somewhere in the Herd-lands, though the likelihood that she survived is slim. It is likely that Dilwun had a wife. Dead or alive, you should find her as well.\n",
[237]="7001CCD4\n1\tCollect boar-meat (total: 10)\030Defeat Blacktusk at Fállug\tBlacktusk and the Mirkwood boars may be found around the ruins of Fállug, west of Amon Angened. Gaerfalas has asked you to hunt Blacktusk and the Mirkwood boars for their meat.\n2\tBring boar-meat to Gaerfalas atop Amon Angened\tGaerfalas is at the way-post atop Amon Angened, east of Fállug. You should bring the boar-meat you collected to Gaerfalas and tell him of Blacktusk's defeat.\n",
[238]="70049125\n1\tDefeat the spirit of the watching stone\tThe watching stone is in Ered Lithui. You should defeat the spirit of the watching stone.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated the spirit of the watching stone.\n",
[239]="7003EDBB\n1\tSearch for some sign of survivors outside Isengard\tSurvivors might be found along the road out of Nan Curunír to the north-west of the Westfold. You have received word of vast destruction at Isengard, and seek to investigate the aftermath in search of any survivors.\n2\tSearch for some sign of survivors outside Isengard\tSurvivors might be found along the road out of Nan Curunír to the north-west of the Westfold. You have received word of vast destruction at Isengard, and seek to investigate the aftermath in search of any survivors.\n",
[240]="7005943C\n1\tCollect driftwood (total: 10)\tDriftwood can be found on the shores of the Brandywine, near Trader's Wharf. You should collect driftwood for the League of the Axe.\n2\tReturn to Tegwen Spurrey with the driftwood you have collected\tTegwen Spurrey can be found at Trader's Wharf. You should return to Tegwen Spurrey with the driftwood you have collected.\n",
[241]="700216A3\n1\tCollect mead from The Plough and Stars\tThe Plough and Stars is in Brockenborings in the Shire. You should speak with Halson Tubwort in Brockenborings, who sells mead, which shall be brought to Nathalan cleverly disguised as Swill.\n2\tBring the fake Swill to Nathalan in Aughaire\tNathalan is in Aughaire, a town of Angmar. You should deliver the \"Swill\" -- actually mead -- to Nathalan.\n",
[242]="7000E8F8\n1\tCollect Swill from the Forsaken Inn\tSwill can be purchased in the Forsaken Inn in the Lone-lands. An Inn League Tavern Keep has asked you to fill a delivery order for some Swill from the Forsaken Inn for an Inn League member stranded all the way in Angmar.\n2\tBring the Swill to Nathalan in Aughaire\tNathalan is in Aughaire in Angmar, far to the north of the Lone-lands. Nathalan told you of his belief that for one to truly appreciate the character of a drink, it must be drank in surroundings that match its character. As a suitable drink for Angmar, he has asked you to collect the worst drink in all of Eriador: \"Swill.\" This drink can only be found at The Forsaken Inn in the Lone-lands.\n",
[243]="700586CD\n1\tBring the letter to Bardag Hailhand at the Shadowed Refuge\tBardag Hailhand is at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone, in Moria.\n2\tPunch an echoing deep-stone and defeat whatever evil is drawn to the sound\tBardag Hailhand described a location north-east of the lake in the Foundations of Stone where he wants you to punch deep-stones and defeat creatures attracted to the echoes.\n3\tPunch an echoing deep-stone and defeat whatever evil is drawn to the sound\tBardag Hailhand described a location north-east of the lake in the Foundations of Stone where he wants you to punch deep-stones and defeat creatures attracted to the echoes.\n4\tPunch an echoing deep-stone and defeat whatever evil is drawn to the sound\tBardag Hailhand described a location north-east of the lake in the Foundations of Stone where he wants you to punch deep-stones and defeat creatures attracted to the echoes.\n5\tPunch an echoing deep-stone and defeat whatever evil is drawn to the sound\tBardag Hailhand described a location north-east of the lake in the Foundations of Stone where he wants you to punch deep-stones and defeat creatures attracted to the echoes.\n6\tPunch an echoing deep-stone and defeat whatever evil is drawn to the sound\tBardag Hailhand described a location north-east of the lake in the Foundations of Stone where he wants you to punch deep-stones and defeat creatures attracted to the echoes.\n7\tTalk to Bardag Hailhand at the Shadowed Refuge\tBardag Hailhand is at the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone, in Moria.\n",
[244]="7004E842\n1\tCollect coils of rope (total: 6)\030Collect water-skins (total: 6)\030Collect bedrolls (total: 6)\tCoils of rope, waterskins, and bedrolls can be found throughout the Hall under the Mountain, including the New-lodes of Narathâk. Dori has asked you to collect coils of rope, waterskins, and bedrolls in preparation for the coming journey to the Grey Mountains.\n2\tDeliver the coils of rope, water-skins, and bedrolls to Dori in Nori's home\tDori can be found inside Nori's home in Tumnuguhûd, the Dwelling-halls of Erebor. You have gathered several coils of rope, water-skins, and bedrolls and should now deliver them to Dori at Nori's home.\n3\tPrepare packs for Dori and Company ([see journal]/6)\tPacks can be found throughout Nori's home in Tumnuguhûd, the Dwelling-halls of Erebor. Despite finding only four willing companions to join him on the journey to Thikil-gundu, Dori has asked you to prepare six packs in the event that Nori is found before he reaches the Steel Keep.\n4\tTalk to Dori in Nori's home\tDori can be found inside Nori's home in Tumnuguhûd, the Dwelling-halls of Erebor. You have prepared all of the packs for Dori and Company. You should now speak to Dori.\n5\tMeet Dori and Company outside Erebor after dusk\tOnce night has fallen, Dori and Company can be found outside the gates of Erebor. Hoping to preserve the secrecy of their journey, Dori has asked the company to join him outside the gates of Erebor after dusk.\n6\tTalk to Dori\tOnce night has fallen, Dori and Company can be found outside the gates of Erebor. You have arrived outside the gates of Erebor to find Dori and Company assembled under a tree beside the River Running. You should speak to Dori.\n7\tPick up the share of Dori's treasure\tOnce night has fallen, Dori and Company can be found outside the gates of Erebor. While Dori and the others begin their journey into the Ered Mithrin, Dori has asked you to deliver a share of his treasure to the ravens of Ravenhill in the hope that he might sooner learn of Nori's whereabouts. You should collect the share of Dori's treasure and prepare to travel to Ravenhill.\n8\tTalk to Arcah at Ravenhill\tArcah can be found at Ravenhill to the south-west of Erebor. Dori has bidden you deliver a share of his treasure to the ravens at Ravenhill. You should ride swiftly and deliver the treasure to the raven-chief, Arcah.\n9\tRavens can be found at Ravenhill to the south-west of Erebor. Arcah has accepted the share of Dori's shiny treasure in exchange for sending a few of her unkindness into the Ered Mithrin to seek for Nori. You should direct ravens to take flight and make for the Ered Mithrin.\t\n10\tFind Dori and Company on the road into the Ered Mithrin\tDori and Company can be found along the road into the Ered Mithrin. You have earned the aid of Arcah's conspiracy and should now follow the road into the Ered Mithrin to rejoin Dori and Company.\n11\tTalk to Dori at Furuk-mekhem, the Southgate\tDori and Company can be found along the road into the Ered Mithrin. You have discovered Dori and Company resting before a large stone structure along the road into the Ered Mithrin. You should talk to Dori.\n",
[245]="700071A0\n1\tCollect Dourhand axes (total: 8)\tThe Dourhands can be found within the ruins of Thandobel, south of Refr Quicksilver. The Dourhand dwarves have forsaken their ties to their brethren by consorting with Orcs. Refr Quicksilver has asked you to bring vengeance upon the Dourhands in the name of the Free Peoples and to bring him a trophy of their axes.\n2\tDeliver the Dourhand axes to Refr Quicksilver\tRefr Quicksilver waits for you at the entrance to the cave, south of the Great East Road in the Lone-lands, north of Thandobel. You should return to Refr Quicksilver with news of your victory against the Dourhands and bring him the axes you took as trophies.\n",
[246]="700076B1\n1\tMost of the smiths of Bree dwell near the West-gate or are working at Thornley's farm along the Greenway. Lofar has told you that he thinks his latest blade was stolen by one of the Man-smiths. He thinks that a warrior, such as yourself, might intimidate the thief into confessing and returning the stolen blade.\t\n",
[247]="700330ED\n1\tDiscover Durin's Court\030Light braziers as you make your way to Durin's Court (total: 6)\tGúthi can be found in Durin's Court, east from Feggi's camp in Ânghumu-ru, and then south through Hadâd-mezer. Unlit braziers can be found along the way. You should make your way across the Flaming Deeps to Gúthi, lighting the braziers along the way.\n2\tTalk to Gúthi at Durin's Court\tGúthi can be found in Durin's Court in the south-eastern Flaming Deeps. You should speak with Gúthi.\n",
[248]="7002F891\n1\tConvince the first merchant to maintain fair prices\030Convince the second merchant to maintain fair prices\030Convince the merchant Léodrim to maintain fair prices\tThe traders and merchants reside at the trader's outpost along the road west from Elthengels. Ofrith has asked you to speak with the other merchants and see that their practices remain fair to both seller and buyer.\n2\tTalk to Ofrith at the merchant-camp\tOfrith can be found at the trader's outpost, west of the village of Elthengels. Ofrith awaits word of the merchants' agreement to demand only fair prices of travellers and refugees.\n",
[249]="70015E14\n1\tSet a false trail\tThe place you should set a false trail lies to the south-west of Limlaer and west of Porth Cadlus. Limlaer has asked you to set false trails for the scouts of the Enemy to find.\n2\tTalk to Limlaer\tLimlaer is south-west of Echad Dúnann, along the Nan Sirannon road. You should return to Limlaer and inform him that the false trail has been set.\n",
[250]="70055177\n1\tBurn fungal mushrooms in the Wracking-hall (total: 10)\tThe Wracking-hall can be found in the Circle of Death. You have discovered a number of fungal mushrooms in the Wracking-hall and should burn them before the fungus can take hold of Minas Morgul.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have burned many fungal mushrooms in the Wracking-hall.\n",
[251]="70027B0D\n1\tTalk to Ondor in the Pit of Iron\tOndor the Dwarf might be within the Orc-cavern in the northern Heathfells. You should find Ondor the Dwarf and return his pick-axe to him.\n",
[252]="7002F913\n1\tShow the locket to Cyneswith\tCyneswith awaits at the farmer's estate to the east, with his son Sager. Cyneswith may be able to tell you more about the locket you found, engraved with his name.\n",
[253]="7002F99A\n1\tCollect phials of Nink-hai acid from Nink-hai defilers\tOrc-defilers can be found in the Nink-hai camp south-east of Faldham. The acids being carried by the defilers should be removed from the possession of the Nink-hai tribe.\n2\tCollect phials of Nink-hai acid (total: 6)\tOrc-defilers can be found in the Nink-hai camp south-east of Faldham. The acids being carried by the defilers should be removed from the possession of the Nink-hai tribe.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have removed many of the acid-phials from the possession of the Nink-hai. The Orcs' acid will not be used against the inhabitants of Faldham.\n",
[254]="700431BB\n1\tDefeat foes in Nud-melek, in Moria (total: 10)\tEnemies can be found throughout Nud-melek, the eastern levels of Moria. Bingo wanted you to defeat foes in Nud-melek as you make your way to the western side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm.\n2\tMeet Bingo at the western side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm\tBingo wanted to meet you at the western side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm, in Nud-melek.\n3\tTalk to Bingo on the west side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm\tBingo is at the western side of the Bridge of Khazad-dûm.\n4\tDefeat foes in Nud-melek, in Moria (total: 10)\tEnemies can be found throughout Nud-melek, the eastern levels of Moria. Bingo wanted you to defeat foes in Nud-melek as you make your way to the exit of Moria.\n5\tPass into Nanduhirion from the First Hall in Nud-melek\tBingo is ready to see the sunlight once again, and wants to meet you in the Dimrill Dale. The exit from Moria is east of the First Hall, in Nud-melek.\n6\tTalk to Bingo outside the East-gate of Moria, in Nanduhirion\tBingo is outside the East-gate of Moria, in Nanduhirion.\n7\tTalk to Spalvi outside the East-gate of Moria, in Nanduhirion\tSpalvi has fallen behind, and stands by the East-gate of Moria, in Nanduhirion.\n8\tTalk to Bingo outside the East-gate of Moria, in Nanduhirion\tBingo is outside the East-gate of Moria, in Nanduhirion.\n",
[255]="70031827\n1\tTalk to Tóla at Lord Ingmar's house\tTóla is at Lord Ingmar's house in the northern part of Eaworth. Ingmar has asked you to let his wife, Tóla, know that he has decided to lead his men against Maustazg, regardless of his father's will.\n2\tTalk to Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tReeve Ingbert is at the Mead Hall of Eaworth, south of Ingmar's home. Tóla requested that you speak with Ingbert and see if he can bring reason to Ingmar.\n",
[256]="70044516\n1\tMeet Bereneth before the Houses of Healing\tThe Houses of Healing are in the Sixth Circle, on the northern side. Bereneth seems to be scared of going into the Houses of Healing by herself and would like you to accompany her. You can meet her before the entrance.\n2\tBring Bereneth to her father\tBereneth's father lies wounded within the Houses of Healing, which are on the northern end of the Sixth Circle.\n3\tTalk to Bereneth\tBereneth will go with you in the Houses of Healing. If you should get separated from her, use Bergil's whistle to call her back. You should talk to Bereneth and reassure her about her father.\n4\tTalk to Araslant\tBereneth's father, Araslant lies recovering in the Houses of Healing. If you should get separated from Bereneth, use Bergil's whistle to call her back. Talk to Bereneth's father and try to learn how ill he is.\n5\tBring Araslant the cup of water\tThe water cup is in Araslant's room in the Houses of Healing. Bring Bereneth's father, Araslant, the cup of water for him to drink.\n6\tTalk to Araslant\tBereneth's father, Araslant lies recovering in the Houses of Healing. If you should get separated from Bereneth, use Bergil's whistle to call her back. Talk to Bereneth's father now that he's had something to drink.\n7\tTalk to the healer Delion\tDelion is in his ward in the Houses of Healing. If you should get separated from Bereneth, use Bergil's whistle to call her back. Find Delion the Healer and let him know Bereneth's father needs his help.\n8\tDelion's ward is within the Houses of Healing in the Sixth Circle. If you should get separated from Bereneth use Bergil's whistle to call her back. Delion will get to Araslant if you attend to some of the other wounded men in his ward.\t\n9\tTalk to Delion\tDelion is in his ward in in the Houses of Healing. If you should get separated from Bereneth use Bergil's whistle to call her back. You should let Delion know you have attended to the wounded and ask him again to attend to Araslant.\n10\tTalk to Bereneth\tBereneth will go with you in the Houses of Healing. If you should get separated from her, use Bergil's whistle to call her back. Talk to Bereneth and see what she wants to do.\n11\tReturn to Araslant\tAraslant lies in a ward of the Houses of Healing in the Sixth Circle. If you should get separated from Bereneth use Bergil's whistle to call her back. You should go back with Bereneth and let Araslant know that the healer will be with him soon.\n12\tTalk to Bereneth\tBereneth will go with you in the Houses of Healing. If you should get separated from her, use Bergil's whistle to call her back. Talk to Bereneth and see what she has to say.\n13\tVisit the Greensward\tThe Greensward lies before the Houses of Healing in the Sixth Circle. Visit the Greensward with Bereneth. If you should get separated from her, use Bergil's whistle to call her back.\n14\tTalk to Bereneth\tBereneth will walk with you in the Sixth Circle. If you should get separated from her, use Bergil's whistle to call her back. Talk to Bereneth and see what she wishes to do next.\n15\tPick flowers (total: 6)\tThe Greensward lies before the Houses of Healing in the Sixth Circle. Pick flowers for Bereneth on the Greensward. If you should get separated from her, use Bergil's whistle to call her back.\n16\tTalk to Bereneth\tBereneth will walk with you in the Sixth Circle. If you should get separated from her, use Bergil's whistle to call her back. Talk to Bereneth and see what she wishes to do next.\n17\tFind Shadowfax\tThe High Stables are just north of the Pier in the Sixth Circle. Go with Bereneth to visit Shadowfax in the High Stables. If you should get separated from her, use Bergil's whistle to call her back.\n18\tTalk to Bereneth\tBereneth will walk with you in the Sixth Circle. If you should get separated from her, use Bergil's whistle to call her back. You have found Shadowfax, Gandalf's steed. Talk to Bereneth.\n19\tTake an apple from the crate\tThe High Stables are just north of the Pier in the Sixth Circle. Take an apple from the crate in the High Stables to feed Shadowfax.\n20\tFeed Shadowfax the apple\tThe High Stables are just north of the Pier in the Sixth Circle. Feed Shadowfax an apple in the High Stables.\n21\tTalk to Bereneth\tBereneth will walk with you in the Sixth Circle. If you should get separated from her, use Bergil's whistle to call her back. Talk to Bereneth and see what she wishes to do next.\n22\tReturn to Araslant\tAraslant lies recovering in the Houses of Healing. If you should get separated from Bereneth, use Bergil's whistle to call her back. Return to Bereneth's father, Araslant, and to see if he is still asleep.\n23\tThe Houses of Healing are in the Sixth Circle, on the northern side. Go around Araslant's ward in the Houses of Healing and hand out the flowers you picked to the other wounded soldiers.\t\n24\tReturn to Araslant\tAraslant lies recovering in the Houses of Healing. If you should get separated from Bereneth, use Bergil's whistle to call her back. Now that you have given out the flowers, you should return to Bereneth's father, Araslant.\n25\tTalk to Bereneth\tBereneth will walk with you in the Sixth Circle. If you should get separated from her, use Bergil's whistle to call her back. Talk to Bereneth and see what she wishes to do next.\n26\tMeet Bereneth back at the Old Guest-house\tThe Old Guest-house lies in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates. Meet Bereneth back at the Old Guest-house.\n",
})
